ASP.NET Core 9/10 Razor Pages + minimal APIs. UseStatusCodePagesWithReExecute re-runs the pipeline on /error/{status} and keeps the original status code unless the error page changes it (docs); UseStatusCodePagesWithRedirects would answer 302 and then 200, a soft-404 trap, so never use it. Status pages only act on responses with an EMPTY body, so return NotFound() / Results.StatusCode(...) before writing anything. UseExceptionHandler re-executes with the ORIGINAL HTTP method, hence the page below handles POST too and skips antiforgery validation (without [IgnoreAntiforgeryToken] an exception in a token-less POST endpoint answered 400 instead of 500 in a test run). Keep the layout free of database queries and session reads (an error page that throws is a second error). In Development the developer exception page shows stack traces: deploy with ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Production (SEC-007). Verify with `curl -i`: unknown URL 404, /old-page 410, database down 503.
